WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:15.413
Having changed into her old but still pretty blue dress and pulled back her damp hair into a tidy bun,

2
00:00:15.414 --> 00:00:19.549
Amy was once again the eager hostess ready to greet her guests.

3
00:00:19.550 --> 00:00:23.780
She waited and waited worriedly for any signs of the arrival of the girls.

4
00:00:23.781 --> 00:00:29.647
But an hour or so later, after the rain had stopped and short bursts of sunshine had broken through the clouds,

5
00:00:29.648 --> 00:00:33.402
not a single guest had appeared at the March home.

6
00:00:33.403 --> 00:00:40.440
Amy wrung her hands, her face crumbling in disappointment as she craned her neck for any familiar faces on the street.

7
00:00:40.441 --> 00:00:47.926
Her family stood a little behind her, aching to console her but letting her retain some dignity.

8
00:00:47.927 --> 00:00:51.331
It was obvious the party was ruined.

9
00:00:51.332 --> 00:00:56.188
"Just wait till I get my hands on those sissy, prissy, no-good brats,"

10
00:00:56.233 --> 00:01:04.427
Jo mumbled under her breath, cracking her knuckles as she pondered ways to get revenge on those who had hurt her sister.

11
00:01:04.428 --> 00:01:08.806
"Jo! You're not helping the situation," Mother whispered loudly.

12
00:01:08.807 --> 00:01:14.935
"Well, I don't think we'll be having any guests today," Amy called out with forced cheeriness.

13
00:01:14.936 --> 00:01:18.881
"Maybe they got lost," suggested Beth kindly.

14
00:01:18.882 --> 00:01:23.931
Amy let out an ugly laugh and said, "I doubt it, dear sister.

15
00:01:23.932 --> 00:01:27.836
More likely they all agreed not to come to teach me a lesson."

16
00:01:27.837 --> 00:01:31.425
"It's because they're jealous of you," offered Jo.

17
00:01:31.426 --> 00:01:36.278
"You're beautiful and talented, and you have a family that adores you."

18
00:01:36.279 --> 00:01:45.061
Shaking her head Amy said, "Thanks, Jo, but it's plain to see that the girls want me to know my place . . . that I don't belong among them.

19
00:01:45.062 --> 00:01:54.109
They let me visit their mansions and castles, as if they're doing me a favor, but they won't set foot in a humble home like ours."

20
00:01:54.110 --> 00:02:00.538
Father wrapped his arm around Amy and said, "I'm not excusing those girls for how they hurt you today, dear,

21
00:02:00.539 --> 00:02:07.341
but whatever their reasons were, don't lose your self-worth or your pride in who you are."

22
00:02:07.342 --> 00:02:14.248
"Thank you, Father, and all of you, for your help and for bearing with me," Amy smiled sheepishly.

23
00:02:14.249 --> 00:02:17.419
"I know I've been such a bother this week."

24
00:02:17.420 --> 00:02:23.870
"It was our pleasure," Mother replied, giving Jo a stern look before she could say anything.

25
00:02:23.871 --> 00:02:27.898
"Now, what are we going to do with all this food?"

26
00:02:27.899 --> 00:02:32.993
Over at the newlyweds' house, Meg's day was not faring any better than Amy's.

27
00:02:32.994 --> 00:02:36.922
John had invited some of his friends over for dinner that evening.

28
00:02:36.923 --> 00:02:41.467
Although Meg had felt confident when she had agreed to prepare a meal all by herself,

29
00:02:41.468 --> 00:02:46.975
she was wondering now how on earth she had gotten herself into such a pickle.

30
00:02:46.976 --> 00:02:53.920
"Two cups of butter, no, one cup butter and one cup oil, no, that doesn't sound right . . .

31
00:02:53.921 --> 00:03:00.313
Oh! I don't know. I can't remember!" Meg cried as she tried to recall the ingredients in apple pie.

32
00:03:00.314 --> 00:03:07.587
Frustrated, Meg decided to make the creamed chicken first but could not find a clean pot to make the sauce in,

33
00:03:07.588 --> 00:03:11.469
because all her dishes were either dirty or being used.

34
00:03:11.470 --> 00:03:15.966
At home, Meg had always relied on Hannah to wash the dishes while she cooked,

35
00:03:15.967 --> 00:03:21.623
and another person to help her prepare the vegetables or hand her the ingredients she needed.

36
00:03:21.624 --> 00:03:28.632
As the mistress of her own home and without a helper (John's modest salary did not allow them to hire someone at the moment),

37
00:03:28.633 --> 00:03:33.212
Meg had to do everything on her own and it was driving her mad.

38
00:03:33.213 --> 00:03:37.694
"Oh! I should just tell John to cancel tonight's dinner. I can't do it!"

39
00:03:37.695 --> 00:03:42.830
said Meg, dropping into a chair, where she held her head and began crying.

40
00:03:42.831 --> 00:03:48.556
A light gentle rap on the window, then a louder one, forced Meg to look up with red eyes.

41
00:03:48.557 --> 00:03:55.079
Jo was peering in with a worried expression, mouthing something Meg could not understand.

42
00:03:55.080 --> 00:03:59.922
Wiping her tears, Meg stood up and opened the door to let her sister in.

43
00:03:59.923 --> 00:04:05.025
"What's the matter, Meg?" Jo demanded, taking hold of her sister's hand.

44
00:04:05.026 --> 00:04:08.597
"I'm so glad to see you, Jo," sniffed Meg.

45
00:04:08.598 --> 00:04:11.225
"How is everything going with Amy's luncheon?"

46
00:04:11.226 --> 00:04:15.909
Snorting loudly, Jo explained what had happened while Meg listened intently.

47
00:04:15.912 --> 00:04:20.585
"Poor Amy!" Meg said, forgetting her own plight at once.

48
00:04:20.586 --> 00:04:27.586
"Yes, but our Amy is a fighter," said Jo proudly, "and she's already put this incident behind her.

49
00:04:27.587 --> 00:04:31.817
She'll be fine. Now what is going on here?"

50
00:04:31.818 --> 00:04:36.941
"I'm such a horrible wife!" Meg began, tears forming again.

51
00:04:36.942 --> 00:04:42.959
"Don't say such things. That's not true. Tell me how I can help," said Jo.

52
00:04:42.960 --> 00:04:47.727
Meg explained what she was doing and why things weren't going as smoothly as she'd like.

53
00:04:47.728 --> 00:04:56.277
"I didn't want to ask you or Mother since I knew Amy needed your help, and besides, I thought I could manage on my own," Meg said.

54
00:04:56.278 --> 00:05:03.319
"Why doesn't John help you?" asked Jo, still looking for an excuse to dislike the man who had taken Meg away from her.

55
00:05:03.320 --> 00:05:12.146
"I'm afraid I'm to blame since I sent him out early this morning on a few errands because I didn't want him to get in my way," Meg said, shamefaced.

56
00:05:12.147 --> 00:05:18.291
As Jo sized up the situation, she realized that Meg was in trouble and desperately needed help.

57
00:05:18.292 --> 00:05:24.108
In a flash, Jo had a great idea. "Meg," she said excitedly.

58
00:05:24.109 --> 00:05:29.779
"Clean up this mess, clean yourself off, put on your lovely dress, and leave the rest to me."

59
00:05:29.780 --> 00:05:35.481
"Jo, are you out of your mind? The guests will be here in two hours," Meg said impatiently.

60
00:05:35.482 --> 00:05:40.815
"Please, Meg, I have an idea. Just trust me," Jo begged.

61
00:05:40.816 --> 00:05:43.538
Meg stared at her sister warily.

62
00:05:43.539 --> 00:05:49.152
Something about Jo's voice and manner persuaded Meg to trust her, so she did as Jo asked.

63
00:05:49.153 --> 00:05:54.902
After cleaning up the kitchen and washing the dishes, Meg took a long bath and changed her clothes.

64
00:05:54.903 --> 00:06:04.632
With no sign of Jo, Meg anxiously tidied her small living room and set out he cutlery and china plates purchased with Aunt March's generous wedding gift.

65
00:06:04.633 --> 00:06:09.883
Then she paced the kitchen floor, her heart racing as her eyes skimmed the bare table.

66
00:06:09.884 --> 00:06:15.793
Meg was beginning to feel sorry for John, who would be coming home to find nothing ready for his guests,

67
00:06:15.794 --> 00:06:21.180
when her ears picked up the sounds of a horse trotting, then stopping in front of the house.

68
00:06:21.181 --> 00:06:25.890
Looking out, Meg burst out laughing at the comical sight.

69
00:06:25.891 --> 00:06:34.012
An old horse was pulling an older wagon with great effort while the passengers, her sisters, waved enthusiastically from the cart.

70
00:06:34.013 --> 00:06:41.777
"Delivery for Mrs. Meg Brookes!" Jo shouted as she jumped out and, grabbing a few baskets, headed toward Meg's open door.

71
00:06:41.778 --> 00:06:47.750
Amy and Beth followed suit and soon, after several trips, because there was a lot to carry in,

72
00:06:47.751 --> 00:06:52.767
Meg's kitchen and dining room table were filled with the lavish food prepared for Amy's party.

73
00:06:52.768 --> 00:06:57.809
"Oh, girls! I don't know what to say!" Meg cried, her eyes shining brightly.

74
00:06:57.810 --> 00:07:02.070
"We can't possibly eat all this food ourselves," said Amy.

75
00:07:02.071 --> 00:07:08.014
"It looks like a feast fit for a king," Meg praised. "John will be so pleased."

76
00:07:08.015 --> 00:07:11.208
"We make a good team, don't you think?" asked Jo.

77
00:07:11.209 --> 00:07:19.015
"We sure do," said Amy. "Through thick and thin, we March girls know how to stick together."
